# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and applies these headers to what it serves.
#
# Why it exists: pages were being served from browsers' caches after a new
# version had gone live, so changes looked like they hadn't deployed when they
# had. "no-cache" does not mean "never store" — it means the browser must ask
# the server whether its copy is still current before reusing it. So repeat
# visits stay quick (the server answers "still fine, use yours"), but you can
# never be shown yesterday's page.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The board and the settings check must never come from a cache at all.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
